    "translation": "The first time I had a job interview for a part-time position was the summer of my third year of high school. The bakery near my house was looking for staff, and I worked up the courage to call. On the day of the interview, I arrived at the shop ten minutes early with my resume, but my hands were cold with nervousness.\nThe manager's questions were simple ones: \"Why do you want to work at this shop?\" and \"How many days a week can you come?\" But what stayed with me most were his final words: \"What matters here is not knowledge about bread, but being able to come in properly every morning.\" Skills can be taught later, he said, but the habit of keeping time depends on the person.\nIn the end, I worked at that shop for two years. I was never late, not even once. Even now, whenever I start something new, I remember those words. I believe trust is born not from special ability, but from keeping small promises every day.",
