    "translation": "I love books, and the shelves in my room were always full. When I moved house, troubled by the weight of the boxes of books, I decided to try e-books. I had carried as many as ten heavy boxes, and both my arms and my spirit were worn out.\nOnce I tried them, I found many convenient points. Even if you load hundreds of books, your bag gets no heavier, and if you feel like reading something, you can buy it right away, even in the middle of the night. Since you can change the size of the characters, they are easy to read even on days when your eyes are tired.\nOn the other hand, I cannot forget the good points of paper books. The feel of turning pages and the pleasure of seeing finished books lined up on the shelf are things e-books do not have.\nThese days, I buy books to read while out as e-books, and books I want to reread many times on paper. Rather than choosing one or the other, I think it is fine to use each according to the purpose.",
